00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,414
Question nineteen.

2
00:00:01,414 --> 00:00:07,384
Step one: macro scan. It asks the size of the uncompressed monochrome image.

3
00:00:07,384 --> 00:00:10,761
One mark. Command words: “file size about”.

4
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:12,175
Step two: denoise.

5
00:00:12,175 --> 00:00:19,401
Useful, in yellow: one thousand twenty-four by seven hundred sixty-eight, one bit per pixel.

6
00:00:19,401 --> 00:00:25,371
In cyan: “uncompressed” and “one K B equals one thousand twenty-four bytes”.

7
00:00:25,371 --> 00:00:27,963
Useless: none — the stem is lean.

8
00:00:27,963 --> 00:00:29,377
Step three: draft.

9
00:00:29,377 --> 00:00:34,797
One thousand twenty-four times seven hundred sixty-eight: total bits.

10
00:00:34,797 --> 00:00:36,603
Divide by eight: bytes.

11
00:00:36,603 --> 00:00:40,609
Divide by one thousand twenty-four: ninety-six K B.

12
00:00:40,609 --> 00:00:41,945
Step four: P O E.

13
00:00:41,945 --> 00:00:46,972
A, seven hundred sixty-eight K B: forgot divided by eight — cut.

14
00:00:46,972 --> 00:00:51,135
B, one thousand twenty-four K B: random number — cut.

15
00:00:51,135 --> 00:00:55,141
C, one hundred ninety-two K B: wrong divisor — cut.

16
00:00:55,141 --> 00:01:04,095
Step five: sanity check and lock. Seven hundred sixty-eight kilobits divided by eight is ninety-six — right scale.

17
00:01:04,095 --> 00:01:06,216
So the correct answer is D.

